# Oracle: VD cmd-save (directives accumulate; default, v(), i(), p(inst, var), hierarchical
# names quoted); run e5 (`default` holds every node voltage and every branch current, an
# inductor's included: all_v + all_branch_i; `save v(b)` governs op, its sweeps and tran, not
# ac; `full` is every unknown, internal nodes included: Private, P2308); `dv` is the ac's own
# directive, which no probe kind states (P2308); `clear saves` drops every save before it (run sv2: Private, P2314, A27).
# A22: the set of kinds a line governs is stated exactly (op, its sweeps, tran; with `default`
# and no p() also ac and dcinc, whose own directive `default` is).
# codes: P2308 P2308 P2314 S0002 S0002 S0002
file "save.sim" deck
  title "save directives"
  save analysis=(op dc tran) (all_v) (all_branch_i) (v (a)) (i (v1)) (param (r1) (i)) (v (x1 n))
  opaque vacask private "save full"
  opaque vacask private "save dv(a)"
  opaque vacask private "clear saves"
